      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I have actively avoided going into group public instances because of the behavior from the moderators in them, constantly breathing down your neck willing to kick you for simply \"looking at someone funny\" or \"having the wrong voice\" or some nonsense like that. Not to mention VRChat putting these instances to the top of the world list by default so you're more likely to join those if not paying attention.\n\nThis update will make it even easier than it already was to get moderator tools in an instance as you won't need VRChat plus anymore to make a group. Previously they had mentioned they don't want to add AI labels to prevent targeted attacks and such, but with these new moderated publics people can do exactly that for ANYTHING at ANY TIME.\n\nQuest user? Kicked. Mute? Kicked. Under 25? Kicked. OVER 25? Kicked. Transgender? Kicked. Have a boyfriend or girlfriend? Kicked. Doesn't have full body? Kicked.\n\nI'm sure you get the point.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
