      "restoredAt": null,
      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I have been discussing the related topic of why I think world authors shouldn't have moderation privileges in all instances of their world for 3 years now, in [remove-world-creator-moderation-powers](https://feedback.vrchat.com/feature-requests/p/remove-world-creator-moderation-powers). While I might have become more willy to compromise on what were to happen with \"Public\" instances, this is a change that I hadn't even considered and I fully welcome it.\n\nIf the random person that made the instance is such a bad person that they start power tripping, I fully believe that almost all of us would simply have left the instance by the time their supposed power trip leads them to kicking us. So if anything, this would lead us to get out of bad instances faster and to find a new better one or make our own instances.\n\nNot to mention that you will likely still find plenty of Public instances where the owner simply left hours ago. But maybe it would be useful for that to be highlighted somewhere in the instance list UI?\n\nMost of all, I see this whole feature as a really good thing for world where the owner of the instance might be considered the host. Such as manually run games or minor event instances. This will allow new VRChat users to use those types of worlds and have some control over the instances without needing to get VRC+ and create a group.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
