      "value": "@{610d538d5303a82960a415b4|full_name} \"If the random person that made the instance is such a bad person that they start power tripping, I fully believe that almost all of us would simply have left the instance by the time their supposed power trip leads them to kicking us\"\n\nWhen the owner just doesn't like you and decides to kick you, you'll have to try to convince your friends to go to another instance, and might not even be able to. It's not that simple as \"if the moderation is bad just leave\". You'll also lose contact with people you just met but hasn't added yet.\n\nI believe it just doesn't scale well to smaller playerbases\n\nI mean, the entire brazilian community only hangs out in TWO specific worlds, there is just no groups of brazilians in other worlds, never. \n\nIt scales with the group issues i have been dealing and reporting for years. There is a lot of toxic groups in the brazilian community, abusing power and banning people for absolutely no reason, and it just prevents you from playing the game since the entire community only stays in these specific places. You can't join your friends, who don't have anything with this, nor any idea of it.\n\nIt'll also be pretty easy for a single user to open multiple public instances of these specific worlds and stay there until it fills and have like 3 instances on his hands. I'm not exaggerating. A few years ago there was a user who monopolized one of these only two worlds we frequent, by buying vrc+ in all his alts and creating different instances of his own. I did reported it, it lasted for months, AND VRCHAT DID NOTHING.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
