      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{60411ec5cc01c21febdcbe37|full_name} How can you make a fanfic about reasons I get kicked only from what has been said here? 💀\n\nBut i can list you a lot of them that happened with me and my friends:\n\nKicked because the mod didn't liked my voice;\n\nBanned because i removed the group owner from my friendlist (he was too toxic and too simp);\n\nFriend banned because he said \"balls\" in the chatbox;\n\nFriend kicked from another group not related to the one above because he said \"balls\" in the chatbox;\n\nA lot of friends banned because they were frequenting instances of a \"rival\" group;\n\nFriends banned because they were representing a group the instance owner didn't liked (nothing offensive or innapropriate);\n\nFriend banned because the mod discovered the person don't like him;\n\nQuest user banned because the owner didn't wanted to explain him his avatar was using suggestive clothings in pc version (while the quest user itself had no idea, it was just toxic, he was being cooperative);\n\nBanned because asked the mods to kick the kids;\n\nFriend banned because used the water droplets emoji (mutually, and only him got banned (a mod steped in and called it \"webrape\"));\n\nFriend banned for absolutely no reason two times from the same group (one ban got lifted after a month complaining to the owner, which he himself couldn't give a reason but was being lazy to unban), and, after less than a week, banned again for no reason.\n\nAnd this.. This happened just too many times to count: group mods flying around a closed group of friends SEARCHING for reasons to ban them. Any intimate joke? Any quick (and non global) sound effect? Any quick (and non global) visual effect? Literally, anything. Instead of playing the actual game, instance moderators are looking for reasons to exercise power;\n\nBanned because spawned prints in the world (nothing offensive or innapropriate).\n\nThere is more.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2026-11-06T00:46:42.442Z",
  "deleteID": null,
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "So, I just read the VRChat dev Update from today (https://ask.vrchat.com/t/developer-update-5-november-2026/49298), \n\nand it says VRChat is going to give Mod permissions to the person who opens a public instance.\n\nI'll be honest here:\n\nIS VRCHAT BLIND? Public instances are the only sanctuaries we could be safe from the Discord Moderador Epidemy that is going on since Groups have been added, and VRChat is getting rid of it by giving mod permissions to the person who opens it??\n\nEven today i got kicked for absolutely no reason because one of these Group Instance moderadors abusing power, and, where did i had to go next? a Public instance, the only place this shit doesn’t happens\n\nThis change just confirms VRCHAT IS NOT LOOKING AT THE POWER ABUSE EPIDEMY. I have already made reports on instance moderators abusing power and VRChat never did anything, even when I had video proofs. And now we get this... This is just insane.",
